.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints, publishes, lists, prunes, and verifies DANE TLSA records.
It emits
.Sy TLSA 3 1 1
.Pq DANE-EE, SubjectPublicKeyInfo, SHA-256
from a live TLS certificate or a local PEM/DER file by default; see
.Fl -usage , -selector ,
and
.Fl -matching
under
.Cm generate
for other parameters.
.Pp
.Ar zone
is the DNS zone
.Pq for example Sy example.com .
.Ar ports
is one port or a comma-separated list
.Pq Sy 443
or
.Sy 25,465 .
.Fl -hostname
is the short host without the zone:
.Sy mx
becomes
.Sy mx.example.org .
The owner name looks like
.Dl _<port>._tcp[.<hostname>].<zone>
.Pp
.Fl -starttls
selects the plaintext upgrade before TLS:
.Sy smtp , imap , pop3 , xmpp ,
or
.Sy none
for implicit TLS.
When omitted, ports
.Sy 25
and
.Sy 587
use SMTP,
.Sy 143
IMAP,
.Sy 110
POP3, and
.Sy 5222
and
.Sy 5269
XMPP
.Pq 5269 uses the server-to-server stream namespace .
Every other port, including 443, 465, 993, and 995, uses implicit TLS.
.Fl -starttls Sy none
forces implicit TLS on a STARTTLS port;
.Fl -starttls Sy smtp
.Pq or imap / pop3 / xmpp
forces that protocol on a nonstandard port.
Certificate verification is disabled on purpose so an expired or
otherwise untrusted leaf can still be hashed.
.Pp
Publisher flags
.Fl -cloudflare ,
.Fl -nsupdate ,
.Fl -route53 ,
.Fl -google ,
and
.Fl -azure
are mutually exclusive.
Credentials and file formats are documented in
.Xr gentlsa 5 .
.Sh OPTIONS
These flags apply to every command:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Print each processing step to standard error
.Pq connect, STARTTLS, handshake, DNS lookup, publisher APIs .
Regular output stays on standard output, so
.Cm verify
remains Nagios-safe.
.It Fl -json
Print one JSON object on standard output instead of text.
.Fl -verbose
can still be combined; steps stay on standard error.
.It Fl -timeout Ar seconds
Deadline for hostname resolution, TCP connect, STARTTLS,
the TLS handshake, and DNS
.Pq including DNSSEC .
Default 30.
A timed-out
.Cm verify
exits UNKNOWN.
Set this below the Nagios service check timeout.
It bounds network work, not the lifetime of the process: the budget is
re-armed after each
.Cm rollover
wait and after
.Fl -reload ,
which are deliberate and can run for hours.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss generate
Fetch the live certificate and print a zone-file style TLSA record.
With a publisher flag, publish that hash.
If a TLSA record already exists, the new hash is added and the old
one is kept
.Pq DANE key rollover .
Use
.Fl -replace
to overwrite instead.
Publishing to a zone with no DS record prints a warning on stderr:
DANE clients ignore TLSA records in an unsigned zone.
.Pp
.Fl -usage , -selector ,
and
.Fl -matching
select other TLSA parameters
.Pq default 3 1 1 .
With usage 0 or 2
.Pq trust anchor ,
the first issuer certificate the server presents is hashed instead of
the leaf.
Publishing is limited to 3 1 1 records; other parameters are
print-only for now.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -hostname Ar name
Short hostname without the zone.
.It Fl -mx
Look up the zone's MX records and generate a record for each exchange
host.
Conflicts with
.Fl -hostname .
An MX outside the zone is printed but cannot be published here.
An unreachable exchange is reported and skipped rather than aborting
the run; the exit status is still non-zero.
The MX RRset is DNSSEC-validated; an unauthenticated one warns on
stderr, because a forged MX answer lets an attacker choose the host
whose key you would then pin
.Pq RFC 7672 Sy \(sc2.2 .
.It Fl -starttls Ar proto
STARTTLS protocol
.Pq Sy smtp , imap , pop3 , xmpp ,
or
.Sy none .
Default is inferred from the port.
SMTP
.Sy EHLO
sends the connection's own source address as an RFC 5321
.Sx 4.1.3
address literal.
For XMPP the stream's
.Sy to=
attribute and the TLS SNI are the zone, not the host connected to, as
RFC 6120
.Sx 4.7.2
requires the XMPP domain there.
.It Fl -info
Print leaf-certificate details before the record.
.It Fl -cloudflare , Fl -nsupdate , Fl -route53 , Fl -google , Fl -azure
Publish via that provider.
.It Fl -replace
With a publisher, overwrite the existing TLSA instead of adding a
rollover hash.
.It Fl -dryrun
With a publisher, print the action but do not write records.
.El
.Ss list
Show TLSA records from DNS.
Publisher flags also print what that provider has.
.Fl -nsupdate
queries the configured primary, or AXFR when
.Ar ports
is omitted.
.Fl -starttls
is used when
.Fl -info
fetches the live certificate.
.Fl -info
fetches the live certificate and marks each
.Sy 3 1 1
hash current or stale.
Other usage/selector/matching values are listed with their RFC 7218
names and are not compared to the live key.
Omit
.Ar ports
to include every port.
.Ss prune
List, and with a publisher delete, TLSA records that no longer match
the live certificate.
Run this after a rollover has been live longer than the DNS TTL.
.Fl -mx
prunes each MX host, as in
.Cm generate .
.Fl -starttls
controls how the live certificate is fetched, as in
.Cm generate .
.Fl -dryrun
shows what would be removed without writing.
.Ss rollover
Publish a not-yet-live certificate hash, wait two TLSA TTLs
.Pq RFC 7671 ,
run
.Fl -reload ,
wait two TTLs again, then prune hashes that no longer match the live
certificate.
A publisher flag is required.
.Fl -replace
is not available.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -hostname Ar name
Short hostname without the zone.
.It Fl -starttls Ar proto
STARTTLS protocol used when checking whether the new certificate is
already live and when pruning.
Persisted on the job so
.Fl -resume
uses the same protocol.
.It Fl -info
Print certificate details.
.It Fl -cloudflare , Fl -nsupdate , Fl -route53 , Fl -google , Fl -azure
Publish, wait, and prune via that provider.
.It Fl -reload Ar cmd
Command to run after the first wait so the service presents the new
certificate.
Without this flag, only the new hash is published and the remaining
steps are printed.
Do not prune before the service presents the new cert.
.It Fl -ttl Ar seconds
TLSA record TTL.
Each wait is twice this value.
Defaults are 300 seconds for Cloudflare
.Pq auto TTL
and 3600 seconds otherwise.
.Ar 0
skips both waits
.Pq unsafe on a live resolver .
.It Fl -schedule
Write the job and start
.Sy gentlsa-rollover@JOB
so the hook does not block.
Requires
.Fl -reload .
.It Fl -dryrun
Print the sequence without writing records, sleeping, or running
.Fl -reload .
.It Fl -resume Op Ar job
Resume a pending rollover after a reboot.
With no argument, resume every job.
.Ar job
may be a job id or a zone
.Pq Sy example.com
or
.Sy example.com_443 .
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl -reload ,
a job is written under
.Pa /var/lib/gentlsa/rollover
if that directory can be created, otherwise
.Ev GENTLSA_STATE_DIR
or the user data directory
.Pq Pa ~/.local/share/gentlsa/rollover
on Linux,
.Pa ~/Library/Application\ Support/gentlsa/rollover
on macOS.
.Cm rollover Fl -resume
continues from the saved deadlines.
After a reboot the new cert is usually already live; resume notices
that, skips
.Fl -reload ,
and only waits until it is safe to prune.
.Pp
Linux RPM and deb packages ship
.Pa gentlsa-resume.service ,
.Pa gentlsa-resume.timer ,
and
.Pa gentlsa-rollover@.service .
Enable the timer after install:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
systemctl enable --now gentlsa-resume.timer
.Ed
.Pp
.Fx ,
Homebrew, and the curl installer do not ship units.
On
.Fx ,
call
.Nm Cm rollover Fl -resume
from cron or
.Sy @reboot .
.Ss verify
Compare every TLSA record in DNS at the owner name with the live
certificate chain.
Nagios-compatible.
Each record is evaluated with its own parameters: usage 1/3 against
the leaf, usage 0/2 against every presented certificate, selectors
0/1, matching types 0/1/2
.Pq hash presence only, no PKIX or DANE-TA chain validation .
After a hash match, remaining days until
.Sy notAfter
are checked against
.Fl -warn
.Pq default 14
and
.Fl -critical
.Pq default 7 .
.Fl -critical
cannot be greater than
.Fl -warn
.Pq rejected with exit 3, UNKNOWN .
.Fl -no-expiry-check
skips the expiry check and restores the hash-only verdict.
A hash mismatch stays ERROR even if the cert is also expiring.
.Pp
The TLSA records are also validated with DNSSEC, locally from the root
trust anchor, through the system resolver.
A DANE client only honors TLSA records that validate as secure, so an
unauthenticated RRset is WARNING and a bogus one is CRITICAL.
A resolver that strips DNSSEC records makes every zone look
unauthenticated; point the system resolver at a full resolver or pass
.Fl -no-dnssec-check .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -hostname Ar name
Short hostname without the zone.
.It Fl -mx
Look up the zone's MX records and verify each exchange host.
Conflicts with
.Fl -hostname .
The MX RRset is DNSSEC-validated as well as the TLSA records: an
unauthenticated MX RRset is WARNING and a bogus one is CRITICAL, even
when the TLSA records themselves validate, because whoever forges the
MX answer picks the host and can sign a TLSA for a key they hold
.Pq RFC 7672 Sy \(sc2.2 .
The overall exit is the worst result.
.It Fl -starttls Ar proto
STARTTLS protocol used to fetch the live certificate, as in
.Cm generate .
.It Fl -info
Print the live certificate before the status line.
.It Fl -warn Ar days
WARNING when the live certificate expires in this many days or fewer.
.It Fl -critical Ar days
CRITICAL when the live certificate expires in this many days or fewer.
.It Fl -no-expiry-check
Check the TLSA hash only, ignoring certificate expiry.
Conflicts with
.Fl -warn
and
.Fl -critical .
.It Fl -no-dnssec-check
Skip DNSSEC validation of the TLSA records.
.El
.Pp
With a port list, the overall exit is the worst result by Nagios
severity: CRITICAL, then WARNING, then UNKNOWN, then OK.
.Ss file
Print the same TLSA data from a local PEM or DER certificate.
Certificate details are shown by default.
.Fl -usage , -selector ,
and
.Fl -matching
work as in
.Cm generate ;
for a trust-anchor record pass the CA certificate file itself.
Pass
.Fl -port
and
.Fl -hostname
to include the owner name.
With a publisher flag, and with
.Fl -zone
and
.Fl -port ,
publish that file's hash before reloading the service.
.Ss completions
Print a shell completion script for
.Ar shell
.Pq Sy bash , zsh , fish , powershell , No or Sy elvish
on stdout.
The RPM, deb, and FreeBSD packages install the bash, zsh, and fish
scripts already; other install methods need it written to the right
directory by hand.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gentlsa completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/gentlsa.fish
.Ed
.Ss cloudflare , nsupdate , route53 , google , azure
Publisher helpers.
.Fl -info
prints authentication status
.Pq never secrets .
.Fl -listzones
lists zones available to the configured account
.Pq implied for Cm cloudflare
when
.Fl -info
is omitted.
