.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Cm verify
uses Nagios-compatible codes.
Other commands exit 0 on success and non-zero on error.
.Bl -tag -width 3n
.It 0
OK.
At least one DNS TLSA hash matches, and the cert expires after
.Fl -warn
days.
.It 1
WARNING.
Hash matches, days left less than or equal to
.Fl -warn ,
or the TLSA or MX records are not DNSSEC-authenticated.
.It 2
CRITICAL.
Hash matches but the cert is expired, not yet valid, or expires
within
.Fl -critical
days, or the TLSA or MX records failed DNSSEC validation
.Pq bogus ;
or ERROR, DNS has TLSA records and none match.
.It 3
UNKNOWN.
Lookup or connection failed, or
.Fl -critical
is greater than
.Fl -warn .
.El
.Pp
.Fl -json
keeps the same exit codes and puts the result in
.Sy status
.Pq Sy ok , warning , critical , error , unknown ,
.Sy message ,
and
.Sy exit .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print a live TLSA record:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gentlsa generate example.com 443
_443._tcp TLSA 3 1 1 0856752f53199a673dcc955c137fe1f5b105a180528acb320bb3eddf15103a9b
.Ed
.Pp
SMTP STARTTLS for
.Sy smtp.gmail.com:587 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gentlsa generate gmail.com 587 --hostname smtp --info
.Ed
.Pp
IMAP on the well-known port, or SMTP on a nonstandard port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gentlsa generate example.com 143 --hostname imap
$ gentlsa generate example.com 2525 --hostname mx --starttls smtp
$ gentlsa generate example.com 25 --starttls none
.Ed
.Pp
Nagios-style verify:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gentlsa verify www.freebsd.org 443
OK - TLSA is valid
.Ed
.Pp
Every MX host for a mail domain on port 25:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gentlsa verify example.com 25 --mx
.Ed
.Pp
Automated DANE rollover after issuing a new certificate
.Pq do not reload the service first :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gentlsa rollover /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.com/cert.pem \\
    example.com 443 --cloudflare \\
    --reload "systemctl reload nginx" --schedule
.Ed
.Pp
Certbot deploy hook
.Pq Pa /etc/letsencrypt/renewal-hooks/deploy/gentlsa :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/bin/sh
set -eu
zone=$(basename "$RENEWED_LINEAGE")
gentlsa rollover "$RENEWED_LINEAGE/cert.pem" "$zone" 443 \\
  --cloudflare --reload "systemctl reload nginx" --schedule
.Ed
.Pp
Use
.Ic certonly
so certbot does not reload in the same run as issuance.
